ing no Netlify functions. It seems I must simulate real data.\n\n\n**Clarifying Real Data**\n\nI\'m now considering existing data sources. I see `downloadedItems` is stored in local state in `EventProcessPage.tsx`, which offers a clue. I need to get *real* data. While I\'m still restricted to `AdminLogin.tsx`, I\'m exploring accessing `localStorage` to potentially pull analytics data. I\'m focusing on \"configures el dashboard para que todos los datos sean reales\" and wondering if I can leverage `localStorage.getItem(\'sepri_analytics\')` within the dashboard itself, since it\'s the only page I can change.\n\n\n**Evaluating Data Extraction**\n\nI\'m now contemplating the most viable approach. Replacing mock data with a `useEffect` in `AdminLogin.tsx` that attempts a fetch from a hypothetical analytics endpoint or local storage seems possible. I\'m torn between using a Netlify function (`/.netlify/functions/analytics`) or `localStorage.getItem(\'sepri_analytics\')`. I\'m struggling with the mandate to avoid changing other files, especially `dataService.ts` and `App.tsx`, which seems necessary for actual tracking. Am I violating the directive to \"solo configurar el dashboard\"? It feels like I can create a tracker function and tell the user that the tracking logic needs to be added elsewhere, or I can just create the Netlify function `analytics.ts` and update `AdminLogin.tsx`, and assume the tracking will be added later.\n\n\n**Refining Data Access**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus and realized I *can* leverage existing data. I can fetch real data (events, news) directly from `dataService` within `AdminLogin.tsx` to generate metrics on the dashboard, even if I cannot create new trackers. Total downloads and visits remain un-trackable. I\'ll modify the dashboard to read data from `localStorage` under a key like `sepri_analytics_data`.\n\n\n**Interpreting Data Source**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in. The directive is crystal clear: I can only touch `AdminLogin.tsx`. The goal is to mak